<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · song</p><h1 class="enc-title">Chhaap Tilak Sab Chheeni</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">14th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Also known as छाप तिलक सब छीनी</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">&quot;Chhaap <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bal-gangadhar-tilak">Tilak</a> Sab Chheeni&quot; is a 14th-century song in Braj Bhasha. It is credited to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sufism">Sufi</a> mystic <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amir-khusrau">Amir Khusrau</a> as both poet and composer, and is one of his most popular compositions, heard across the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indian-subcontinent">Indian subcontinent</a>. It is sung above all as qawwali, the devotional music of the Sufis, by Pakistani and Indian qawwals and other singers.</p></div>
